    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler_tests.parse_environment_decode_roundtrip", decl_name: "base_compiler", field: WholeDeclaration }
  ],
  reason: "The required floor judges three base-revision facts (cost-debt roster, parse environment, kernel-name set) and evaluated them with the HEAD seed, so a head that deletes a builtin the base calls made the base unevaluable (gunbc#13378, which blocked the v2 single-authority migration of from_code_point). That is the PURPOSE test of gunbc.v1_maintenance_standing v1_seed_standing: the change serves the v2 self-host program by letting the seed's own builtins be deleted as v2 authorities replace them, without each deletion breaking the floor. The floor runner the facts feed is seed Rust (v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner, namespace_baseline), and the base side must run inside the BASE revision's binary, which is the seed claim_executor the merge queue already builds; so the cross-revision contract, its typed refusals, the verb that answers it and the three rerouted call sites are seed Rust beside the runner they serve. The fetch, verify, retention and wait are .dag (gunbc.compiler_gate_workflow, gunbc.fleet_desired_candidate, gunbc.fleet_release_bins_key).",
  owning_dissolution_lane: "v1-hand-queue-drain" as RoadmapNodeId,
  trigger: "Delete these items when the required floor's base-side reads run as v2 .dag folds behind the native CLI door (v2.cli.compile_cli, std.compiler_entry NativeCliDriver): the base-fact contract (schema, fact names, refusal arms) declared in .dag, the base side answered by the base revision's emitted CLI, and the head side consuming it from the floor's .dag fold. Sufficient only if all three facts migrate with the refusals intact (no head-seed fallback, unknown schema refuses, mismatch refuses); moving the verb without the refusals is not admissible.",
  current_boundary: "gunbc.compiler_gate_workflow base-compiler fetch/verify steps -> GUNBC_BASE_COMPILER* job env -> v1_compiler.cli_run.base_facts base_fact_from_base_compiler -> base revision's claim_executor --base-fact -> v1_compiler.cli_run.base_facts emit_base_fact"
}
